16 year old samish John has been  training as a mechanic at the shop in  Istanbul for a few months three years  ago his parents divorced his mother was  forced to find a job to support him but  when turkey's inflation skyrocketed he  decided to drop out of school  even if you have two people earning  minimum wage salaries life is difficult  for that household I give my salary to  my family I also work as a photographer  over the weekends I spend that money for  myself I did not want to force my family  to send me to school especially as a  Young Man  inflation reached 85 percent when the  government cut interest rates at the end  of 2021. in a year Galera has lost more  than twice its value compared to the US  dollar  s runs his 40 year old Dowry shop he  says he's had to increase prices five  times in the past year  inflation is like a monster increases in  the minimum wage don't help people if we  didn't have Arab tourists it would be  too difficult not only for us all of  Istanbul the hotels groceries and  markets  higher rent water and electricity bills  are weighing heavily on the small  business  there are three people working here I  need one more but I can't afford it many  businesses around here have started to  employ Afghan or Syrian refugees  president  announced a total of 80 increase in the  minimum wage this year on top of the 50  high at the end of last year turkey is  gearing up for an election in mid-2023  president erdogan is expected to pump  more money into the economy before the  vote which is likely to lead to more  price increases he also promised to  reduce inflation to 40 percent in a few  months it is unclear how we will manage  both but in the meantime Turkish  citizens are finding it more and more  difficult to make ends meet  Al Jazeera Istanbul
 

